Subject: [PATCH 2/3] front page: the statute is overdue, not early; conform
 the page to the two definitions

The maintainer's catch: the provenance section framed the Act as arriving
BEFORE the catastrophe. That is not this project's position and never was.
The sequence -- incident, hearing, record, statute -- has already run three
steps in frontier AI. The statute is late, not early, and the page now says
so.

- 'Why the statute precedes the catastrophe' -> 'Why this statute is
  overdue'. Rewritten: five disclosed incidents across three developers, one
  learned from the victim; hearings demanded under oath; a congressional
  record whose own text concedes no federal law governs it. Only the fourth
  step is missing, and every other industry that reached this position had
  already buried people.
- 'In one paragraph' gains the scope direction -- the laboratories hold a
  technical definition of frontier, the Act holds a legal one -- while
  stating that none of it is in any tagged text yet.
- 'For sponsors and staff' -> 'For legislative sponsors and staff', with a
  standfirst distinguishing a legislator who carries a bill from a funder,
  and repeating that the project is unfunded and not seeking funding.
- The two twelves disambiguated where the collision actually occurs: on the
  front page, four paragraphs above the coverage table.
- 'A note on fixed headcounts' extended to govern the coverage set: criteria
  applied to public facts, an illustration and never a roster, and the
  statute names no company.
- Structure tree: docs/ was labelled 'retired paths (signposts)' while
  holding five live documents the same page links; research/ was missing
  entirely though it holds the front page's headline exhibits.
- Dead #recent anchor removed (the log moved to the diary on 22 Aug); the
  consolidation paragraph's stale three-file list retired; the Contents
  preamble no longer promises every folder an index it does not have.
- docs/README.md: 'the three long documents' -> five, with the definition and
  known objections indexed.

Tagged v3.4 text unchanged (E10).
